MENTOR: Glow it is. This frame is at 0.5 s, halfway through Glow's Gaussian Blur Blurriness, which changes from 0 s to 1 s.

The blur changes at one steady rate the whole way and then stops dead at 1 s. That's linear, and it's why it looks mechanical. Easing slows the change down as it leaves one key and again as it arrives at the next.

Glow only has that one pair, so if I eased it there'd be nothing left for you to do. With Glow's keys showing (U), select both Blurriness keys and choose **Animation > Keyframe Assistant > Easy Ease** (F9). The diamonds turn into hourglasses.

If you'd like to watch me do one first, Title has four pairs, and I can ease one of those while you do the rest. Otherwise, ease Glow's Blurriness between 0 s and 1 s and say done.
